# A bootable target and explicit assistant access

## Goal

Show what a Nerves target and an assistant (MCP) surface would share with
every other Lab entry point, and which parts already exist: the neutral
design tokens the workbench renders, the schema-versioned evidence record a
target smoke test would emit, and the inert scenario descriptor an assistant
could list. The Nerves firmware, the on-target smoke, the MCP server and
the control plane of WLB.07 and WLB.08 are **planned**: fully specified,
maintainer-owned to publish, and absent from source. The cells below run
only what exists; the planned surfaces are documentation and are marked as
such. The notebook's evidence status is `partial`.

## Prerequisites

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:wotex_lab, "~> 0.1.0"},
  {:nx, "~> 0.13.1"}
])
```

The requirements above are published-artifact requirements. At the time this
notebook was written none of the `wotex*` packages is published on Hex; the
notebook is verified against the workspace source cohort recorded in
`docs/provenance/source-cohort.json` by `test/wotex/lab/cookbook_test.exs`,
which evaluates every Elixir cell below in order (skipping this install
cell). `Mix.install/1` never points at a Git checkout. No firmware is built,
no device is contacted and no assistant is started.

## Package and consumer ownership

| Concern | Owner | Where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Design tokens and scoped CSS | `wotex_lab` (implemented) | `Wotex.Lab.DesignSystem` |
| Evidence record schema, digests, public-content scan | `wotex_lab` (implemented) | `Wotex.Lab.Evidence.Record`, `Digest` |
| Scenario descriptors as data | `wotex_lab` (implemented) | `Wotex.Lab.Scenario` |
| Nerves system, firmware image, on-target smoke | planned delivery lane (WLB.08) | not in source |
| MCP resources, tools, transports, quotas | planned control plane (WLB.07) | not in source |
| Publishing firmware, images, packages | maintainer only | never an agent or a notebook |

## Run

```elixir
alias Wotex.Lab.DesignSystem
alias Wotex.Lab.Evidence.{Digest, Record}
alias Wotex.Lab.Scenario
alias Wotex.Lab.Telemetry
```

The design tokens a workbench on any host, including an embedded one,
renders: versioned, JSON-compatible, with the same roles in both themes and
a scoped stylesheet that pulls in no external asset.

```elixir
tokens = DesignSystem.tokens()
css = DesignSystem.stylesheet()

%{
  version: DesignSystem.version(),
  groups: Map.keys(tokens) |> Enum.sort(),
  same_roles?: Enum.sort(Map.keys(tokens["light"])) == Enum.sort(Map.keys(tokens["dark"])),
  scoped?: css =~ ".wotex-lab" and not (css =~ ":root") and not (css =~ "url("),
  every_token_emitted?:
    Enum.all?(tokens, fn {_group, group} -> Enum.all?(group, fn {name, value} -> css =~ "--wl-#{name}: #{value};" end) end)
}
```

The evidence record an on-target smoke would produce. Every dependency must
state its archive evidence: because no `wotex*` package is published, each
states `archive: :missing` rather than a digest synthesized from a checkout.
The record refuses paths, callbacks, process identities and credentials.

```elixir
{:ok, fixture_digest} = Digest.file(Application.app_dir(:wotex_lab, "priv/fixtures/thermal/thing-description.json"))

dependencies =
  for app <- [:wotex, :wotex_nx, :wotex_runtime, :nx] do
    %{name: Atom.to_string(app), version: to_string(Application.spec(app, :vsn)), archive: :missing}
  end

record_fields = %{
  scenario_id: "nerves-smoke",
  revision: "unrecorded",
  attempt: 1,
  source_tree_digest: Digest.bytes("source tree not digested in this notebook"),
  lock_digest: Digest.bytes("lock not digested in this notebook"),
  dependencies: dependencies,
  fixtures: %{"thermal/thing-description.json" => fixture_digest},
  seed: 42,
  toolchain: Digest.toolchain(Nx.BinaryBackend),
  budgets: %{boot_ms: 60_000, deadline_ms: 5_000},
  inputs: ["fixture:thermal/thing-description.json"],
  assertions: [
    %{id: "WLB-C10:nerves-boot", status: :not_run},
    %{id: "WLB-C10:nerves-reconnect", status: :not_run},
    %{id: "WLB-C08:mcp-resources", status: :not_run}
  ],
  outcomes: %{target: "rpi4", hardware: "unavailable", note: "planned lane; host-only record"},
  durations: %{},
  cleanup: %{status: :ok, details: %{}}
}

{:ok, record} = Record.new(record_fields)
{:ok, record_digest} = Record.digest(record)
{:ok, again} = Record.new(record_fields)
{:ok, again_digest} = Record.digest(again)
{:ok, encoded} = Record.encode(record)
{:ok, decoded} = Wotex.JSON.decode(encoded)
{:ok, read_back} = Record.from_map(decoded)

{record_digest, record_digest == again_digest, Enum.map(read_back.dependencies, & &1.archive), read_back.assertions}
```

The scenario descriptor an assistant would list: data with string ids and
capabilities, a seed and a step budget, and no executable authority.

```elixir
{:ok, scenario} =
  Scenario.new(
    id: "nerves-smoke",
    title: "Boot, run the thermal foundation, reconnect",
    capabilities: ["nx.encode", "nx.evaluate", "nx.decode", "runtime.loopback"],
    seed: 42,
    max_steps: 100
  )

descriptor = Scenario.to_map(scenario)
```

The planned surfaces, shown as documentation only (this block is not an
Elixir cell and is not executed):

```text
# Planned (WLB.08 Nerves lane, implementation_status: planned):
#   MIX_TARGET=rpi4 mix firmware   # pinned Nerves system, toolchain and firmware digest
#   mix burn / mix upload          # maintainer action; the image ships with license and integrity data
#   on-target smoke: boot, Wotex.Lab.Examples.Thermal.run/0, loopback reconnect, evidence record
# Planned (WLB.07 MCP, implementation_status: planned):
#   stdio and Streamable HTTP transports; resources for package/spec/seam/scenario/Thing/evidence
#   metadata; tools for parse, validate, explain error, list/discover/read simulated Things,
#   bounded conformance and benchmark jobs, seam explanations; quotas and cancellation;
#   writes require explicit instance opt-in and per-request authorization.
```

## Deliberate breakage

Public evidence cannot carry a machine path, a callback or a credential; a
dependency that omits its archive field is refused so the absence is always
stated rather than implied.

```elixir
{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: path_code, path: path_pointer}} =
  Record.new(%{record_fields | inputs: ["/tmp/private/fixture.json"]})

{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: secret_code}} =
  Record.new(%{record_fields | outcomes: %{note: "token=abc.def"}})

{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: unstated_code, path: unstated_pointer}} =
  Record.new(%{record_fields | dependencies: [%{name: "wotex", version: "0.1.0"}]})

{:error, %Wotex.Lab.Error{code: scenario_code}} =
  Scenario.new(id: "nerves-smoke", title: "x", capabilities: ["a"], seed: 1, max_steps: 1, module: System)

{path_code, path_pointer, secret_code, unstated_code, unstated_pointer, scenario_code}
```

## Safe telemetry

No Lab span is emitted by tokens, records or descriptors; they are pure
data. The record itself is scanned so that nothing in it could leak through
a log or a label.

```elixir
handler_count = length(:telemetry.list_handlers([:wotex, :lab]))
public? = not (encoded =~ "/Users") and not (encoded =~ "/home") and not (encoded =~ "token=")
{handler_count >= 0, public?}
```

## Expected output

| Check | Expectation |
| --- | --- |
| `tokens-both-themes` | Version `0.1.0`, groups `base`, `dark`, `light`, identical roles in both themes |
| `stylesheet-scoped` | Scoped to `.wotex-lab`, no `:root`, no `url(`, every token emitted |
| `evidence-record-digest` | The canonical digest is stable across two equal records and the record reads back |
| `archive-missing-stated` | Every dependency states `:missing`; an omitted field is `:archive_evidence_unstated` |
| `scenario-descriptor-data` | The descriptor is a string-keyed map with schema version `1.0.0` and hidden execution fields are refused |

```elixir
%{
  "tokens-both-themes" =>
    DesignSystem.version() == "0.1.0" and Map.keys(tokens) |> Enum.sort() == ["base", "dark", "light"] and
      Enum.sort(Map.keys(tokens["light"])) == Enum.sort(Map.keys(tokens["dark"])),
  "stylesheet-scoped" =>
    css =~ ".wotex-lab" and not (css =~ ":root") and not (css =~ "url(") and
      Enum.all?(tokens, fn {_group, group} -> Enum.all?(group, fn {name, value} -> css =~ "--wl-#{name}: #{value};" end) end),
  "evidence-record-digest" =>
    record_digest == again_digest and String.starts_with?(record_digest, "sha256:") and
      read_back.assertions == record.assertions and public?,
  "archive-missing-stated" =>
    Enum.all?(read_back.dependencies, &(&1.archive == :missing)) and unstated_code == :archive_evidence_unstated and
      unstated_pointer == "/dependencies/0/archive" and path_code == :not_public_evidence and
      secret_code == :not_public_evidence,
  "scenario-descriptor-data" =>
    descriptor["schema_version"] == "1.0.0" and Enum.all?(Map.keys(descriptor), &is_binary/1) and
      scenario_code == :invalid_options
}
```

## Public seam

No WoTEx seam is implemented here. The Lab contracts exercised are
`Wotex.Lab.DesignSystem`, `Wotex.Lab.Evidence.Record` and
`Wotex.Lab.Scenario`; the target and assistant surfaces are planned
entries in the generated graph.

## Spec and completion IDs

* Lab: WLB.07 and WLB.08, control plane, MCP and Nerves lane planned
  (`WLB-C08`, `WLB-C10`).
* Upstream: none claimed.

## Replacement adapter

There is no adapter to replace until the lanes exist. A host that builds the
firmware or the MCP server consumes the same three contracts above: render
the tokens, emit records through `Record.new/1`, and list descriptors from
`Scenario.to_map/1`; none of them may be extended with executable fields.
